desktop-shell: publish the window list for the Task Manager

The Task Manager (hexa-taskmgr) shows the open apps in its Apps tab, but
a Wayland client cannot see other clients' windows. The shell already
tracks every top-level window for the taskbar; it now also writes them
to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hexa-windows, one line per window:

    ID<tab>PID<tab>FLAGS<tab>APP-ID<tab>TITLE

ID and FLAGS are the taskbar's (weston_desktop_shell.window). PID is
the owner process: the Wayland client, or _NET_WM_PID for X11 windows
(XWayland, Wine); 0 when unknown. Tabs and newlines in titles become
spaces. The file is rewritten (to a temporary file, then renamed) from
an idle callback after a change, so a burst of title changes costs a
single write; it is removed when the shell stops.

